<h1>Utah Algebraic Geometry Preprint Seminar (Fall 2023)</hl><br>
<hl></h1>
This is the website for the Utah AG preprint seminar, organized by Daniel Bragg and Christopher Hacon. This is a weekly reading seminar on recent (~<2 years old) preprints in algebraic geometry. Each week a speaker will choose a paper to present (not written by themselves). You can find the webpage for the previous semester's iteration of the seminar <a href="./seminar_S23">here</a>.
<br>
<br>
If you would like to be added to the seminar mailing list, send an email to Daniel.
<br>
<br>
If you would like to be a speaker, email Daniel with your desired time slot and paper. See the schedule below for open times. If you would like to talk but don't have a paper in mind, the organizers will be happy to suggest a paper.
<br>
<br>												      
The seminar is scheduled to meet Mondays 3:00-4:00 in LCB 215.
<br>
<br>




